        {
          "name": "lucy_begin_question",
          "description": "Recommended at the start of each new user business question. Prefer the user's original wording in `question`; always provide `intentSummary`. When multiple visible sources may match the same business term, Lucy allows the query but discloses the selection in answer_verifiability.sourceSelection (tell the user which source you used and that it was unconfirmed). source_ambiguity_gate is returned only for hard failures (unresolved refs, catalog health, cross-connection, more than 4 sources, or no source-qualified reference at all while the business term matches several sources); then retry as a single-source query using `source.measure` keys. Skipping begin does not bypass these hard checks. Do not call for protocol checks or tool discovery only.",
          "inputSchema": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "question": {
                "type": "string",
                "maxLength": 2000
              },
              "intentSummary": {
                "type": "string",
                "maxLength": 500
